Optional bounded-workspace prefill and small-query extensions on SM75.

VLLM_TURING_PREFILL_WINDOW=16384 limits FP16 KV staging to 64 MiB; a
pre-profiled FP32 accumulator and LSE merge windows without changing the
attention mask. Earlier windows are fully visible; the final window contains
all query tokens and uses lower-right causality. The 2048-query accumulator
adds 48 MiB. Default 0 retains the original full-context workspace.

VLLM_TURING_EXTEND_MAX=32 uses separately preallocated packed split-KV scratch
for short extensions, without changing speculative QMAX or replaying a decode
model graph. It consumes the live prefill metadata; recurrent-state init is
untouched. Default 0 retains the original dispatch.

Explicit FP32 Hadamard signs are essential: preallocation runs while model
loading has set the default dtype to FP16. All workspace is allocated before
memory profiling, and the knobs participate in vLLM's compilation-cache hash.

Requires the preceding Turing series. Numeric/replay tests:
  python bench/test_turing_prefill.py
Measured performance and remaining limits: docs/turing-prefill.md.

